{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XZ49QLMAZaHdT1Rsf3ySVg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me compile the results:\n\n**APC 300:**\n| | Before | After Run1 | After Run2 | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| STARK excl trace | 1121ms | 1107ms | 1123ms | Within noise |\n| Trace Commit | 197ms | 190ms | 192ms | ~6ms improvement, marginal |\n\n**APC 100:**\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| STARK excl trace | 1308ms | 1305ms | Within noise |\n| Trace Commit | 286ms | 277ms | -9ms, borderline |\n\n\n**APC 0:**\n| | Before | After Run1 | After Run2 | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| STARK excl trace | 1834ms | 1779ms | 1784ms | -50ms, but within noise |\n| Trace Commit | 476ms | 467ms | 463ms | ~10ms improvement |\n\nLooking at APC 0's trace commit results, I'm getting an average of 465ms versus the baseline of 476ms, which is about an 11ms improvement—actually larger than what I saw with APC 300. That's unexpected if the L2 batching was supposed to help APC 300 more. I need to reconsider what's happening at APC 0 with the batching at 49.\n\nAt APC 0, I'm dealing with 49 batches times 3 steps, which means 147 kernel launches compared to just 3, so the L2 cache benefit should be moderate with 4MB columns. The 11ms improvement could be real or just noise. Meanwhile at APC 300, I'm seeing only about 6ms improvement in trace commit (averaging 191ms versus 197ms), which lands at the low end of the 5-15ms improvement the plan predicted. The overall STARK exclusion trace improvement at APC 300 is basically flat—around 1115ms versus 1121ms, well within noise margins. Against the rollback criteria, I'm right on the edge: the trace commit improvement is barely above the 5ms threshold, and there's no regression on STARK at APC 0, so this is a borderline decision.\n\nGiven that the 6ms improvement falls within typical measurement noise and doesn't meaningfully move the needle, I'm treating this as a failed optimization and will proceed with committing the implementation followed by reverting it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":780,"cache_read_input_tokens":75674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":780},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8cac4de4-fad6-4efd-889f-d2a384eb17c5","uuid":"82e713d4-9923-4eeb-aec5-604c026f3ef0"}
